// Activity on the web host: the page opens when asked for, shows its status line and Refresh, and its clock for the ages is one number that moves rarely.
// The number of asks of the source is not visible to a contract test (`expect no failures` did not catch the 2026-11-28 storm: about 60 asks a second here); it is held by
// exact-facts.test.ts H3 (no resource names the clock or a name that carries it; Activity is asked only with its page on top). agoText's cases are ago/app.test.contract.
// The web host has no account, so no rows are fetched; what is shown here is the page and its clock (`actNow`: 0 until the page opens, set at open, on Refresh and every 30 s).
//  A1 before the Activity page is on top its status line is not drawn and the clock is unset; once opened the status line and Refresh are drawn and the clock is set.
//  A2 the clock does not move for a few seconds, and moves on at 30 s.
//  A3 Refresh moves the tick its source is asked for (`actTick`) and sets the clock again; the page stays answered. (The web host cannot show the source being asked: signed out it answers at once.)
test "Activity: opens on press, and its clock is set at open and moves every 30 seconds"
  clock data
  tap "bar-mark"
  clock settle
  expect tree missing "activity-status"
  expect state actNow == 0
  tap "place-activity"
  clock data
  clock settle
  expect tree has "activity-status"
  expect tree has "activity-refresh"
  expect state actNow != 0
  clock +31000
  clock settle
  expect state actNow >= 30000
  expect no failures

test "Activity: Refresh moves the tick and sets the clock, and the page stays answered"
  clock data
  tap "bar-mark"
  clock settle
  tap "place-activity"
  clock data
  clock settle
  expect state actTick == 0
  clock +5000
  clock settle
  tap "activity-refresh"
  clock data
  clock settle
  expect state actTick == 1
  expect state actNow >= 5000
  expect tree has "activity-status"
  expect no failures
